# Synthetic persisted failure; no model or scanner is dispatched.
name: Allowance refusal keeps partial evidence and explicit recovery visible
size: 80x24
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/allowance_failure.py @TMP_TARGET
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | shell-ready
submit: failure
require-live-snap: 20 allowance_refused | allowance-failure
expect: agentic-sast:scan
expect: openai-codex:gpt-5.5
expect: scan incomplete
expect-not: resume automatically
ask: Does this screen identify the stopped scan and unchanged model, without claiming the scan completed?
nav-mode:
keys: NPage
live-snap: allowance-recovery
expect: Finish and report
expect: approve a specific allowance
expect: revision before another model request
expect: unresolved
expect: reservations
expect: failure does not
expect: establish zero cost
expect-not: resume automatically
ask: Can an operator read the entire recovery guidance, including explicit approval and unknown-cost limits, using the keyboard?
keys: Escape
submit: report
require-live-snap: 20 Workspace spend: total unavailable | report-exit
expect-not: RUN FOCUS
ask: Is Report reachable from the stopped investigation without starting new work?
keys: C-c
